{"metric":"thin_shell_wormhole","source":[{"metric":"thin_shell_wormhole","system":"spherical","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"676f48f86a3edd1d"},{"metric":"thin_shell_wormhole","system":"throat","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"618250bdc5c0632f"}],"views":[{"id":"throat","label":"Through the throat","box":[-3.4916,3.4916,-3.3916,3.3916],"system":"throat","caption":["Visser's thin shell wormhole ($a = 1.25\\,r_s$), each point in the diagram a 2-sphere of radius $a + |\\ell|$. The metric on the plane of $t$ and $\\ell$ is $(1 - r_s/r)\\left(-c^2dt^2 + d\\ell_*^2\\right)$, with $\\ell_* = \\ell + r_s\\ln\\left(1 + |\\ell|/(a - r_s)\\right)\\mathrm{sgn}(\\ell)$ running over the whole line, and $p, q = \\arctan((ct \\mp \\ell_*)/r_s)$ bring it into the full diamond.","The two ends are two asymptotically flat universes, each with its own $i^0$ and $\\mathscr{I}^\\pm$, joined at the throat $\\ell = 0$, where the shell sits. The factor $1 - r_s/r$ is at least $1 - r_s/a$ everywhere, so light crosses the throat and there is no horizon."],"layers":[{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[3.1416,0.0],[0.0,3.1416],[-3.1416,0.0],[0.0,-3.1416]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"cover","points":[[3.1416,0.0],[0.0,3.1416],[-3.1416,0.0],[0.0,-3.1416]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[-0.0,-3.1411],[-0.0027,-3.1133],[-0.011,-3.0838],[-0.0446,-3.0188],[-0.1089,-2.9323],[-0.2077,-2.8187],[-0.3537,-2.6625],[-0.5808,-2.4275],[-2.1306,-0.8566],[-2.5813,-0.3901],[-2.7186,-0.2375],[-2.7956,-0.1388],[-2.8212,-0.098],[-2.8376,-0.064],[-2.8474,-0.0324],[-2.851,-0.0008],[-2.8482,0.0285],[-2.8398,0.0581],[-2.826,0.0891],[-2.8047,0.1252],[-2.7434,0.2077],[-2.6424,0.3239],[-2.4921,0.4846],[-2.2566,0.728],[-0.7021,2.3036],[-0.2672,2.7542],[-0.1332,2.9032],[-0.0575,2.9996],[-0.0322,3.0392],[-0.0138,3.0766],[-0.0034,3.11],[-0.0,3.1411]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","poi